Input: {"question": "When was the Ognissanti church completed?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 0, "end": 138, "text": "Ognissanti, Mantua The Ognissanti is a Baroque style, Roman Catholic church located on Corso Vittorio Emanuele in Mantua, Lombardy, Italy."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 139, "end": 264, "text": "It is reputed that Matilde of Canossa granted the Ognissanti church around 1080 to the Abbey of Polirone in San Benedetto Po."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 265, "end": 349, "text": "Others ascribe the donation to the Benedictines as a gift by Pope Adrian IV in 1159."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 350, "end": 479, "text": "The present church and façade were completed by 1755, creating a new church with stood at right angles to the original structure."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 480, "end": 575, "text": "The belltower and the \"chapel of the dead\" retain some of the original Romanesque architecture."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "start": 576, "end": 598, "text": "In 1797, the order was"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d01", "start": 0, "end": 207, "text": "Groundbreaking 12th century Completed 1752-1755 Website www.ognissantisanbarnaba.it The Ognissanti is a Baroque style , Roman Catholic church located on Corso Vittorio Emanuele in Mantua , Lombardy , Italy ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d01", "start": 208, "end": 351, "text": "History [ edit ] It is reputed that Matilde of Canossa granted the Ognissanti church around 1080 to the Abbey of Polirone in San Benedetto Po ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d01", "start": 352, "end": 437, "text": "Others ascribe the donation to the Benedictines as a gift by Pope Adrian IV in 1159 ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d01", "start": 438, "end": 569, "text": "The present church and façade were completed by 1755 , creating a new church with stood at right angles to the original structure ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d01", "start": 570, "end": 587, "text": "The belltower and"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "start": 0, "end": 170, "text": "Ognissanti, Venice Ognissanti (Italian: \"Chiesa di Ognissanti\") is a 16th-century Roman Catholic church located in the Dorsoduro \"sestiere\" of the Italian city of Venice."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "start": 171, "end": 340, "text": "In the 15th century, the area of the current church housed a monastery of Cistercian nuns who had moved here from Torcello, the nearby islands now largely uninhabitable."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "start": 341, "end": 463, "text": "In 1472 a hospice was built with an annexed small church, which is shown in the plan of Venice made by Jacopo de' Barbari."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "start": 464, "end": 537, "text": "This was replaced from 1505 by the current building, consecrated in 1586."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "start": 538, "end": 610, "text": "The church and the nunnery were suppressed by Napoleon Bonaparte in 1807"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "start": 0, "end": 44, "text": "the current building , consecrated in 1586 ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "start": 45, "end": 238, "text": "The church and the nunnery were suppressed by Napoleon Bonaparte in 1807 and left abandoned until Giovan Battista Giustinian [ it ] turned them into a convalescent facility for elderly people ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "start": 239, "end": 421, "text": "Later the monastery became a hospital , active until the mid-1990s , while the church , contained in the former 's perimeter , was used for religious functions for recovered people ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "start": 422, "end": 468, "text": "It now forms part of the Giustinian Hospital ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "start": 469, "end": 571, "text": "[ 1 ] Description [ edit ] The church 's façade is divided into three vertical sectors , corresponding"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04", "start": 0, "end": 235, "text": "Ognissanti, Florence The chiesa di San Salvatore di Ognissanti or more simply chiesa di Ognissanti (; \"Church of All Saints\"), is a Franciscan church located on the piazza of the same name in central Florence, region of Tuscany, Italy."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04", "start": 236, "end": 352, "text": "Founded by the lay order of the Umiliati, the church was dedicated to all the saints and martyrs, known and unknown."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04", "start": 353, "end": 497, "text": "It was completed originally during the 1250s, but almost completely rebuilt around 1627 in Baroque-style by the architect Bartolomeo Pettirossi."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04", "start": 498, "end": 624, "text": "Soon after, a new façade (1637) was erected using designs by Matteo Nigetti, that conserved the glazed terracotta lunette over"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 0, "end": 10, "text": "or water ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 11, "end": 78, "text": "If the painting requires deeper cleaning , consult a professional ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 79, "end": 205, "text": "YOU MAY ALSO LIKE The Rio Ognissanti and the church of the Gesuiti , Venice by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 194.74 Rio St."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 206, "end": 293, "text": "Geronimo , Venezia by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 194.74 A View in Venice , Rio S."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 294, "end": 421, "text": "Marina by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 194.74 Rio Santa Barnaba , Venice by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 194.74 Rio St."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d05", "start": 422, "end": 562, "text": "Barnaba , Venice by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 194.74 A procession in Southern Italy by Franz Richard Unterberger From $ 192.01 Canale"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 0, "end": 47, "text": "the church 's atmosphere is incredibly moving ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 48, "end": 51, "text": "5 ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 52, "end": 112, "text": "Instagram-Worthy : Your followers will love of these shots !"}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 113, "end": 263, "text": "The Architecture : A Feast for the Eyes I have n't talked much about the building itself yet , but the architecture of Ognissanti is worth a mention ."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 264, "end": 365, "text": "The church dates back to the 13th century , though it 's been renovated and expanded over the years ."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 366, "end": 462, "text": "The facade , with its simple elegance , is a great example of Baroque architecture in Florence ."}, "D7S7": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d06", "start": 463, "end": 532, "text": "It was redesigned in the 17th century , giving the church its current"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d00:c0", "entity": "Ognissanti church", "scope": "Mantua", "claim": "The present church and façade of the Ognissanti church in Mantua were completed by 1755.", "answer": "1755", "quote": "The present church and façade were completed by 1755, creating a new church with stood at right angles to the original structure.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d02:c0", "entity": "Ognissanti church", "scope": "Venice", "claim": "The current building of the Ognissanti church in Venice was consecrated in 1586.", "answer": "1586", "quote": "This was replaced from 1505 by the current building, consecrated in 1586.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d03:c0", "entity": "Ognissanti church", "scope": "completion/consecration", "claim": "The current building of the Ognissanti church was consecrated in 1586.", "answer": "1586", "quote": "the current building , consecrated in 1586 .", "original_document_number": 4}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0365-fa0026c7c7b3:d04:c0", "entity": "Ognissanti church", "scope": "original completion", "claim": "The Ognissanti church was completed originally during the 1250s.", "answer": "1250s", "quote": "It was completed originally during the 1250s, but almost completely rebuilt around 1627 in Baroque-style by the architect Bartolomeo Pettirossi